{% doc %}
  Renders two editorial band columns that share the same label as a single
  merged mobile row: one shared label above a side-by-side pair of images
  (Figma's actual mobile frame for this section groups same-label columns
  this way, at a taller fixed image height than the solo 3-across row).
  Desktop has no such pairing in Figma — it renders both columns
  independently there, each with its own repeated label, same as any other
  solo column.

  Each block renders exactly once. From lg up both wrappers below are
  `display: contents`, so the two columns become ordinary items of the
  band's flex row — rendering a separate desktop copy instead would put each
  block's theme-editor attributes on two elements.

  @param {object} block - The first `column` block object
  @param {object} next_block - The second `column` block object, sharing block's label
{% enddoc %}

<div class="editorial-band__column-pair col-span-3 flex flex-col gap-editorial-row-label-gap lg:contents">
  {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
    <span class="editorial-band__label block uppercase font-plex-mono font-bold text-editorial-label-mobile lg:hidden">{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="flex gap-editorial-row-paired-gap-mobile lg:contents">
    {%- render 'editorial-band-column', block: block, paired: true -%}
    {%- render 'editorial-band-column', block: next_block, paired: true -%}
  </div>
</div>
